  "lineage": "Harawi is an old Quechua song genre of the southern Peruvian highlands, sung chiefly by older women at agricultural rites such as sowing and harvest, at weddings, roof-raisings and farewells, in a very high voice with long held tones that fall away at phrase ends. It is usually sung without instruments, and its name gave rise to the colonial mestizo yaraví.",
